From 5d53a5b2a145b6d10972a13303e310bed0a8031b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:26:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] utils: barriers, semaphores and absolute sleeps without glibc

Three POSIX interfaces used on the critical path of every executor do
not exist on Darwin:

  pthread_barrier_t      thread pool start-up synchronisation
  sem_init()             declared, returns ENOSYS; task_ans and the ITTI
                         shutdown wait use it
  clock_nanosleep()      rt_sleep_ns() and the realtime time source,
                         both with TIMER_ABSTIME

  system.c:198:10: error: call to undeclared function 'clock_nanosleep'
  system.c:198:43: error: use of undeclared identifier 'TIMER_ABSTIME'
  task_ans.c:40:3: warning: 'sem_init' is deprecated

Add common/utils/oai_sem.h, a counting semaphore that is sem_t where
sem_init() works and a libdispatch semaphore on Darwin, and switch the
two users to it. Add common/utils/darwin_compat.h, empty outside
Darwin, with pthread_barrier_* over a mutex, a condition variable and a
generation counter, and clock_nanosleep() over nanosleep() with the
absolute deadline converted against the requested clock; it returns the
error number like the Linux call so that a caller retrying on EINTR
recomputes the interval from the same deadline. Include it from the
thread pool header, system.c and time_source.c.
